        "timestamp_display": "02:59",
        "timestamp_seconds": 179,
        "url": null
      },
      "speaker": "Dr Jennifer Tufts",
      "text": "Well, you do a lot. A lot of different things. You rotate in all the different aspects of psychiatry as well as internal medicine so that you have a foundational knowledge of broad medical topics. You admit patients into the inpatient hospital. You manage emergencies in the hospital and in the emergency room. Decide whether patients need to be admitted psychiatrically or not, and also carry a panel of outpatients.",
      "event_types": [
        "admitted"
